# Verification and completion

- Use targeted falsifying tests, implementation, related tests, risk-based PR gates,
  and integrated-main verification.
- Linux/cloud execution cannot claim Windows-native verification.
- Mock, dry-run, component, or local-only evidence cannot claim live unattended operation.
- Require a genuine golden journey covering intake, missing-work selection,
  implementation, tests, governed branch/PR/merge, Jira reconciliation, next-work
  recomputation, restart recovery, and continued work around a HUMAN_REQUIRED lane.
- The unattended qualification ladder is fixture, controlled external writes,
  recovery, 4-hour trial, 24-hour soak, and 72-hour soak.
- Only the deterministic Completion Gate may declare the project complete, and it
  must include passing unattended operating-loop qualification.
